<title>USA: Brent crude creeps up in late U.S. paper trading.</title>
<headline>Brent crude creeps up in late U.S. paper trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Benchmark Brent crude oil creeped up in U.S. paper trading in a quiet Friday afternoon, traders said.</p>
<p>Two partials of July Brent changed hands 100 times apiece at $18.15 and $18.18 a barrel.</p>
<p>The July contract on London's IPE settled at $18.14 a barrel.</p>
<p>June/July Brent traded twice at minus 15 cents, three cents weaker than the lowest deal in London.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
